msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:24
msgid ""
"<span id=\"env-NIX_IGNORE_SYMLINK_STORE\">[`NIX_IGNORE_SYMLINK_STORE`](#env-"
"NIX_IGNORE_SYMLINK_STORE)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:26
msgid ""
"Normally, the Nix store directory (typically `/nix/store`) is not allowed to "
"contain any symlink components. This is to prevent “impure” builds. Builders "
"sometimes “canonicalise” paths by resolving all symlink components. Thus, "
"builds on different machines (with `/nix/store` resolving to different "
"locations) could yield different results. This is generally not a problem, "
"except when builds are deployed to machines where `/nix/store` resolves "
"differently. If you are sure that you’re not going to do that, you can set "
"`NIX_IGNORE_SYMLINK_STORE` to `1`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:36
msgid ""
"Note that if you’re symlinking the Nix store so that you can put it on "
"another file system than the root file system, on Linux you’re better off "
"using `bind` mount points, e.g.,"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:45
msgid "Consult the mount 8 manual page for details."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:47
msgid ""
"<span id=\"env-NIX_STORE_DIR\">[`NIX_STORE_DIR`](#env-NIX_STORE_DIR)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:49
msgid ""
"Overrides the location of the Nix store. On Unix, the default is `/nix/"
"store`, set at compile time by the `libstore:store-dir` build option. On "
"Windows, there is no compile-time setting; the default is `%PROGRAMDATA%"
"\\nix\\store`, determined at runtime using the [`%PROGRAMDATA%` Known Folder]"
"(#known-folders)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:53
msgid ""
"See the [Store Types](../store/types/index.md) chapter; each store has a "
"`store` setting linking back to this as its default."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:55
msgid "<span id=\"env-NIX_LOG_DIR\">[`NIX_LOG_DIR`](#env-NIX_LOG_DIR)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:57
msgid ""
"Overrides the location of the Nix log directory. On Unix, the default is `/"
"nix/var/log/nix`, set at compile time by the `log-dir` build option. On "
"Windows, there is no compile-time setting; the default is `%PROGRAMDATA%"
"\\nix\\log`, determined at runtime using the [`%PROGRAMDATA%` Known Folder]"
"(#known-folders)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:61 source/command-ref/env-common.md:69
msgid ""
"The [Local Store](../store/types/local-store.md), [Local Daemon Store](../"
"store/types/local-daemon-store.md), and [Experimental SSH Store with "
"filesystem mounted](../store/types/experimental-ssh-store-with-filesystem-"
"mounted.md) have per-store settings that override this."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:63
msgid ""
"<span id=\"env-NIX_STATE_DIR\">[`NIX_STATE_DIR`](#env-NIX_STATE_DIR)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:65
msgid ""
"Overrides the location of the Nix state directory. On Unix, the default is `$"
"{localstatedir}/nix`, where `localstatedir` is a compile-time build option "
"defaulting to `/nix/var`. On Windows, there is no compile-time setting; the "
"default is `%PROGRAMDATA%\\nix\\state`, determined at runtime using the "
"[`%PROGRAMDATA%` Known Folder](#known-folders)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:71
msgid ""
"<span id=\"env-NIX_DAEMON_SOCKET_PATH\">[`NIX_DAEMON_SOCKET_PATH`](#env-"
"NIX_DAEMON_SOCKET_PATH)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:73
msgid ""
"Overrides the path to the Unix domain socket used to communicate with the "
"Nix daemon. Defaults to `daemon-socket/socket` within the state directory "
"(see [`NIX_STATE_DIR`](#env-NIX_STATE_DIR))."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:76
msgid ""
"See the [Local Daemon Store](../store/types/local-daemon-store.md) "
"documentation for details on how the socket path is resolved."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:78
msgid "<span id=\"env-TMPDIR\">[`TMPDIR`](#env-TMPDIR)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:80
msgid ""
"Use the specified directory to store temporary files. In particular, this "
"includes temporary build directories; these can take up substantial amounts "
"of disk space. The default is `/tmp`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:84
msgid "<span id=\"env-NIX_REMOTE\">[`NIX_REMOTE`](#env-NIX_REMOTE)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:86
msgid ""
"Overrides the [`store`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-store) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:94
msgid "Nix language evaluator settings"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:96
msgid ""
"<span id=\"env-NIX_SHOW_STATS\">[`NIX_SHOW_STATS`](#env-NIX_SHOW_STATS)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:98
msgid ""
"If set to `1`, Nix will print some evaluation statistics, such as the number "
"of values allocated."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:101
msgid ""
"<span id=\"env-NIX_COUNT_CALLS\">[`NIX_COUNT_CALLS`](#env-NIX_COUNT_CALLS)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:103
msgid ""
"If set to `1`, Nix will print how often functions were called during Nix "
"expression evaluation. This is useful for profiling your Nix expressions."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:107
msgid ""
"<span id=\"env-GC_INITIAL_HEAP_SIZE\">[`GC_INITIAL_HEAP_SIZE`](#env-"
"GC_INITIAL_HEAP_SIZE)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:109
msgid ""
"If Nix has been configured to use the Boehm garbage collector, this variable "
"sets the initial size of the heap in bytes. It defaults to 384 MiB. Setting "
"it to a low value reduces memory consumption, but will increase runtime due "
"to the overhead of garbage collection."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:114
msgid "<span id=\"env-NIX_PATH\">[`NIX_PATH`](#env-NIX_PATH)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:116
msgid ""
"A colon-separated list of search path entries used to resolve [lookup paths]"
"(../language/constructs/lookup-path.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:118
msgid ""
"This environment variable overrides the value of the [`nix-path` "
"configuration setting](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-nix-path)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/env-common.md:120
msgid ""
"It can be extended using the [`-I` option](../command-ref/opt-common.md#opt-"
"I)."
msgstr ""

